	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44354</id><title>International Day for the Eradication of Poverty 2026</title><updated>2026-10-15T18:34:04-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44354" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Int_day_eradication_poverty.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Int_day_eradication_poverty.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Int_day_eradication_poverty-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Int_day_eradication_poverty.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
 
A safe home is more than a roof over our heads. 
It is the foundation of health, security, opportunity and human dignity. 
Yet for billions of people, that foundation remains out of reach.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44354&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “International Day for the Eradication of Poverty 2026”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44349</id><title>Afghanistan’s Stolen Peace: The Women Who Refuse to Be Silenced</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:39:48-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44349" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Zahra-Nader-Editor-in-Chief-Zan-Times_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
BENGALURU, India, October 15 (IPS)  - When the Taliban took control of Afghanistan in August 2021, Zahra Nader was pursuing a doctorate in Women and Gender studies at York University in Canada. Nader had planned to return to Afghanistan to continue her research, possibly teach at Kabul University, and continue exploring Afghan women’s role in political history.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44349&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Afghanistan’s Stolen Peace: The Women Who Refuse to Be Silenced”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44348</id><title>30 Years of War, 30 Years of Impunity in DR Congo</title><updated>2026-10-15T14:22:24-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44348" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/People-continue_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/People-continue_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/People-continue_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/People-continue_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
WASHINGTON DC, October 15 (IPS)  - It has been 30 years since Rwanda-backed rebel forces attacked Lemera hospital in what was then eastern Zaire, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.amnesty.org/es/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/afr620291996en.pdf&quot;&gt;killing&lt;/a&gt; 37 patients and medical staff. This was one of the first major atrocities during what became known as the First Congo War, helping to unleash decades of foreign-backed rebellions and grave abuses against civilians by all sides, including ethnic-based &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/news/2025/08/06/dr-congo-armed-group-massacres-dozens-in-church&quot;&gt;massacres&lt;/a&gt;, widespread &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/01/12/dr-congo-surge-in-conflict-related-sexual-violence&quot;&gt;rape&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/reports/2002/drc/&quot;&gt;sexual violence&lt;/a&gt;, forced &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/report/2026/06/10/death-was-everywhere/arbitrary-detention-killings-and-forced-recruitment-by-the&quot;&gt;recruitment&lt;/a&gt; of children, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/report/2026/05/14/we-are-civilians/killings-sexual-violence-and-abductions-by-the-m23-and-rwandan&quot;&gt;abductions&lt;/a&gt;, torture, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/news/2014/06/10/democratic-republic-congo-ending-impunity-sexual-violence&quot;&gt;mutilation&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrw.org/report/2010/09/14/always-run/vicious-cycle-displacement-eastern-congo&quot;&gt;forced displacement&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44348&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “30 Years of War, 30 Years of Impunity in DR Congo”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44350</id><title>Kenia Hernández: Indigenous Rights Defender Imprisoned for Her Activism</title><updated>2026-10-15T10:42:37-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44350" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Kenia-defensora.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Kenia-defensora.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Kenia-defensora-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Kenia-defensora.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
JOHANNESBURG, South Africa, October 15 (IPS)  - Kenia Hernández is an Indigenous Mexican lawyer and human rights defender dedicated to advancing women’s rights and social justice.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44350&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Kenia Hernández: Indigenous Rights Defender Imprisoned for Her Activism”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44359</id><title>Could your brain data be used against you? UN calls for limits on neurotechnology</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44359" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Brain signals recorded by a gaming headset or a wellness gadget could one day be used as evidence against you in court, according to a new UN report which warns that neurotechnology is outpacing the laws meant to protect human rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44359&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Could your brain data be used against you? UN calls for limits on neurotechnology”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44358</id><title>World losing ground in ‘war on nature’ as progress on biodiversity targets lags</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44358" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/27-08-2021-UNDP-Myanmar-livelihoods.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/27-08-2021-UNDP-Myanmar-livelihoods.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/27-08-2021-UNDP-Myanmar-livelihoods.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/27-08-2021-UNDP-Myanmar-livelihoods.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fewer than half of the national targets set to protect the world’s plants, animals and ecosystems are on track, the UN warns in a new report, days before countries gather in Yerevan, Armenia, for the COP17 biodiversity conference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44358&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “World losing ground in ‘war on nature’ as progress on biodiversity targets lags”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44357</id><title>Afghanistan faces record hunger levels amid rampant rights violations</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44357" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/30-06-2025-WFP-Afghanistan-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/30-06-2025-WFP-Afghanistan-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/30-06-2025-WFP-Afghanistan-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/30-06-2025-WFP-Afghanistan-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acute malnutrition and hunger in Afghanistan have reached the highest levels ever recorded, with 15.9 million people facing acute food insecurity and conditions set to worsen in the coming months, according to a global hunger monitor report released on Thursday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44357&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Afghanistan faces record hunger levels amid rampant rights violations”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44356</id><title>AI, green energy and economic transitions risk leaving vulnerable communities behind, UN warns</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44356" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/23-09-2024-UNICEF-India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/23-09-2024-UNICEF-India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/23-09-2024-UNICEF-India.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/23-09-2024-UNICEF-India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rapid transformations – from artificial intelligence and digital technologies to renewable energy and demographic shifts – are reshaping economies worldwide, creating new opportunities but also threatening to deepen socio-economic inequalities, a new UN report warned on Thursday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44356&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “AI, green energy and economic transitions risk leaving vulnerable communities behind, UN warns”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44355</id><title>Ukraine: Critical health supplies destroyed in ongoing Russian attacks</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44355" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/08/28-08-2026-WHO-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/08/28-08-2026-WHO-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/08/28-08-2026-WHO-Ukraine-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/08/28-08-2026-WHO-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ongoing and deadly Russian attacks across Ukraine are causing serious healthcare disruption, with more than $1.5 million-worth of medicines and supplies destroyed in four separate strikes on warehouses used by the UN there since July. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44355&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ukraine: Critical health supplies destroyed in ongoing Russian attacks”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44353</id><title>WHO urges vigilance after Kenya confirms second Ebola case</title><updated>2026-10-15T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44353" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/06-10-2026-WHO-Kenya-Bundibugyo-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/06-10-2026-WHO-Kenya-Bundibugyo-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/06-10-2026-WHO-Kenya-Bundibugyo-03.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/06-10-2026-WHO-Kenya-Bundibugyo-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The World Health Organization (WHO) continues to support Kenya’s efforts to contain Ebola after a second person tested positive for the Bundibugyo virus, the UN agency’s representative in the country said on Thursday. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/15/44353&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “WHO urges vigilance after Kenya confirms second Ebola case”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0053s ch:0 -->